# API Generation System

## Overview
Automatic TypeScript API client generation from Go Fiber backend OpenAPI documentation.

## Workflow
1. **Backend**: Go handlers with Swagger annotations
2. **Generation**: OpenAPI spec → TypeScript client  
3. **Integration**: Type-safe API calls in frontend

## Key Commands
```bash
bun backend:docs   # Generate OpenAPI docs only (fast)
bun gen-api       # Full pipeline: docs → TypeScript client → build (complete)
```

## Generated Package Structure
```
packages/api/
├── src/              # Generated TypeScript source
│   ├── apis/        # API endpoint classes
│   ├── index.ts     # Main exports
│   └── runtime.ts   # HTTP client runtime
└── dist/            # Built JavaScript + type declarations
```

## Adding New Endpoints

### 1. Backend (Go)
```go
// endpoint godoc
// @Summary Short description
// @Description Detailed description
// @Tags category
// @Accept json
// @Produce json
// @Param data body ModelType true "Description"
// @Success 200 {object} ResponseType
// @Router /path [method]
func handlerName(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // Implementation
}
```

### 2. Generate Client
```bash
bun gen-api
```

### 3. Frontend Usage
```typescript
import { ApiClass } from '@decm/api';

const api = new ApiClass({
  basePath: 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1'
});

const result = await api.methodName(); // Fully typed!
```

